{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What to review\n     6\t\n     7\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \"Forecast unavailable\"\n     8\trelease. The governing documents:\n     9\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\n    10\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\n    11\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\n    12\t\n    13\tCode that the design reuses:\n    14\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\n    15\t  `ladder_bands`;\n    16\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\n    17\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\n    18\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\n    19\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\n    20\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Questions\n    23\t\n    24\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\n    25\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\n    26\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\n    27\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Name any path with a stored example.\n    30\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\n    31\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\n    32\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\n    33\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\n    34\t   forecast restated in different words?\n    35\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\n    36\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\n    37\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\n    38\t   - groups left out;\n    39\t   - the sweep floor.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Decide each.\n    42\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\n    45\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Not ready to build.** On macOS, an empty output folder created after the builder checks the path can be replaced by the final rename. A second problem is reproducible without touching a file: with a legacy ledger whose last judgement is September 20, the resolver accepts an explicit September 21 build, but revision 3 tells `check` to reject that package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:98) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:126](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:126) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) · [Apple’s rename(2) manual](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man2/rename.2.html)\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. The 74b findings\n     4\t\n     5\t| Finding | Revision 3 |\n     6\t|---|---|\n     7\t| **1. Date, class, records and counts** | **Partly closed.** The builder passes its resolved date. The checker derives each class from the stored measure and labels, and compares lists with their multiplicities, so an added record fails. Two gaps remain. **Date:** `check` adds a ceiling that `build` does not apply, detailed below. **Order:** `created_seq` alone does not determine an ordered list. I verified that `old-2/v2` and `v3` both have sequence 8. The existing library breaks ties with `rowid`. Specify that same order for export and verification so two valid queries cannot disagree. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:77](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:77) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:98) · [bundle.py:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:232) |\n     8\t| **2. Missing source item** | **Behaviour closed. Test 13 is still insufficient.** The checker starts from every visible source row, takes its publication day there, and requires its item. But test 13 deletes only the item. A broken inner join would also refuse, because the finished package still contains the source the join dropped. For the decisive case, omit that source from a copy of the package as well, refresh its hash, and require refusal naming the missing item. The inner-join mutant would then accept it. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:114) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:287](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:287) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:305](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:305) |\n     9\t| **3. Regular files and unique JSON member names** | **Closed in the design.** `lstat` checks each of the two entries, and both files reject repeated names at every nesting level. For test 15 to prove the duplicate-name check, its altered data must have a matching manifest hash and a genuine value last in the repeated pair. Otherwise another check can refuse it even after duplicate detection is removed. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:129) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:291](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:291) |\n    10\t| **4. Staging ownership, errors and competing builds** | **Partly closed.** Exclusive, per-build staging resolves ownership. A competing builder’s finished, nonempty package survives. The empty-destination race and two error-handling gaps remain, detailed below. Test 9 also still requires an existing staging folder to block the build, contradicting the new crash-recovery rule. Test 14 should have both builds reach staging before either publishes, so a sequential retry cannot satisfy it. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:122](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:122) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:184) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:274) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:289](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:289) |\n    11\t| **5. Diagnostic columns** | **Closed.** The two optional judgement columns are read only where present, and the report records their absence. I verified that the served ledger has `reasons` and `why_changed` and lacks both `implied_outcome` and `reference`. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339) |\n    12\t| **Builder-refusal test** | **Open.** Test 12 now reaches the right decision and names the right outcomes. Its in-process replacement of `release_export` violates AGENTS §4, which permits fakes only for external services. The scratch-copy test below exercises the real command. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:281) · [AGENTS.md:151](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:151) |\n    13\t\n    14\t### 2. The evidence-summary disagreement\n    15\t\n    16\t**Yes, §8 records it faithfully.** In `e3238`, the source says “more than double” a $20 billion figure. The stored summary attributes “more than $40 billion” to NVIDIA. Both readers agree the arithmetic is faithful and the figure did not come from Hivemind’s judgement. They disagree on whether “amounts as quoted” permits that attribution. Section 8 preserves both readings and identifies keeping the summary alongside the quote as the cheaper, reversible decision. The reported percentages count extra digit sequences across evidence records. They do not establish how often a calculated amount is attributed to a source. [codex-r74b.md:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:18) · [codex-r74b.md:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:20) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:362](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:362)\n    17\t\n    18\t### 3. Changes required before building\n    19\t\n    20\t- **Use one date rule for both commands.** I exercised `service.resolve_bound` against an in-memory ledger with no processing steps or completed days. With a September 20 judgement, its default was September 20 and its explicit September 21 bound passed. With no judgement, the default was `None` and the explicit date still passed. Line 100 turns that default into a ceiling only for `check`, and gives no usable ceiling for the empty case. Use `resolve_bound` for the explicit date on both paths. Keep the build’s equality check against the requested date and its refusal when an omitted date has no default. Test that an explicit legacy package passes a subsequent `check`, and that a date beyond a real completed day still refuses. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) · [service.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:24) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) · [OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:315](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md:315)\n    21\t- **Make the final move itself refuse an existing destination.** An existence check followed by `os.rename` leaves a window in which an empty directory can appear and be replaced. Use an atomic no-replace operation, such as `renamex_np(..., RENAME_EXCL)` on a supporting macOS filesystem, and refuse if the guarantee is unavailable. Exercise the empty-directory case at the move itself. Two builders publishing nonempty packages cannot expose it. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:126](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:126) · [macOS SDK rename.2:139](/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/usr/share/man/man2/rename.2:139) · [Apple’s rename(2) manual](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man2/rename.2.html)\n    22\t- **Put cleanup where the staging path is known, and distinguish failure after publication.** If either file write fails, `write_package` has created staging but has yet to return its path to the caller. It must clean up there, or the caller must acquire staging before the writes. After a successful rename, a report-write error has the opposite outcome: the checked package exists and `check` can regenerate its report. The blanket “no final folder exists” rule gives the wrong recovery action at that point. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:120) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:145) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:150)\n    23\t- **Run test 12 through the real builder on a scratch copy.** Establish that the unchanged command succeeds. On the scratch copy, introduce the already-listed writer fault that substitutes judgement text for one evidence summary. Run the same command and require the origin-mismatch reason, nonzero exit, no output package and removal of its staging folder. Then remove only the staged check while retaining the writer fault. The bad package must reach the destination and make the refusal test fail. This proves exactly which check prevents publication, using the mutation procedure AGENTS §4 already specifies. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:282](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:282) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:296) · [AGENTS.md:158](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:158)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
