{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'def (evidence|evidence_record|read_snapshot|open_read_only|library)|order by created_seq, rowid|sqlite3' src/hivemind/{bundle.py,service.py,views/store.py} | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/bundle.py:14:def read_snapshot(*connections):\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:206:    for row in conn.execute('select * from thesis_groups order by created_seq, rowid'):\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:225:def library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\nsrc/hivemind/bundle.py:232:        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:11:import sqlite3\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:59:    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:60:    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:223:def open_read_only(path):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:229:    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{real}?mode=ro', uri=True, timeout=READ_BUSY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:230:    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:348:    except sqlite3.OperationalError:\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:418:def evidence(conn, evidence_id):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:427:def evidence_in_force(conn, view_id):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:449:def evidence_ids_under(conn, view_id):\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:537:        except sqlite3.OperationalError:\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:584:        except sqlite3.OperationalError:\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:9:import sqlite3\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:85:_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:224:def evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:238:def evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:306:    except sqlite3.Error as error:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '85,107p;145,166p'; rg -n 'atomic|no.replace|folder|directory|staging' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md,codex-r74b.md,round74d-brief.md}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '85,107p;145,166p'; rg -n 'atomic|no.replace|folder|directory|staging' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md,codex-r74b.md,round74d-brief.md}\"","aggregated_output":"    85\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n    86\t- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\n    87\t  proves nothing.\n    88\t- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or recording it, and\n    89\t  cite what you read, not the summary (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？\").\n    90\t\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   145\t## 4. Tests\n   146\t\n   147\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\n   148\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\n   149\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\n   150\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\n   151\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n   152\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\n   153\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\n   154\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\n   155\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n   156\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\n   157\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\n   158\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n   159\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\n   160\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n   161\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\n   162\t  unexercised, not passed.\n   163\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\n   164\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\n   165\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\n   166\t  the inner function with every argument set.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74d-brief.md:8:One design choice differs from 74c's suggestion. Instead of `renamex_np(RENAME_EXCL)`, the build claims its output folder with an\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74d-brief.md:9:atomic `os.mkdir` before any export. The final `os.rename` then lands on its own empty claim. A rename replaces only an empty\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74d-brief.md:11:removes only an empty folder. Judge whether this meets the requirement that no build can replace a folder it did not create, using\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74d-brief.md:19:   - the move cannot replace a folder the build did not create;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74d-brief.md:20:   - cleanup where the staging path is known;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:9:| Build order, retry and budgets | **The order and thresholds are resolved.** The builder checks staging before rename. A report-only failure can be retried against the finished package. Size and time now have thresholds fixed before the first control. A retry can measure its own verification time, but cannot recover the elapsed time of the original export. Its report must distinguish those measurements. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:264](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:264) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:10:| Tests and mutants | **The identity fixtures and dated leak cases are resolved.** The design now distinguishes resolved and unresolved numbers, a genuinely absent key table, and an event with distinctive labels. August 25 and August 28 select the intended judgements. **The builder refusal test remains open.** Test 10 calls the checker directly. Test 11 fails on a missing item *before staging exists*. Both can pass if the builder stops checking staged files before rename. Exercise the builder with a staged origin mismatch and assert nonzero exit, no final package, and removal of its own staging directory. Removing the builder’s check must fail that test. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:223](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:223) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:241](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:241) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:279](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:279) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:27:4. **Give staging one owner through rename.** The table treats an existing staging directory as crash debris, although another build may still be checking it. Specify exclusive staging creation, cleanup only by the invocation that acquired it, and a final move that refuses an existing destination. An ordinary write or rename error also needs a defined outcome. Test two builds aimed at the same output: the losing build must leave the winner’s staging and finished package intact. After a report-only failure, `check` should leave the checked package in place and report only the measurements it can reproduce. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:101) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:119) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:150)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
