{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"web_search","id":"exec-18cc786d-12b1-4377-bef1-7ef76d692572","query":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.rename","action":{"type":"open_page","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.rename"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.python.org","ref_id":"turn0view0","snippet":"Total lines: 4163","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/i8Ve9XZoDFqz2c1oUOE5VDdRGV-PDRuLkp256Bobx5OKlYr_GZcq61J2iEpLkZ-RK9y6pq_ivZm0LgaPEGi6I_30ZBm09fr_v6guC1DToSbN2VQAaEDVsGKg0wiB8XHX_cmZwaOzztSSCGt4k9QCOA","title":"os — Miscellaneous operating system interfaces — Python 3.15.2 documentation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.python.org","ref_id":"turn0view1","snippet":"Total lines: 4163","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/ujl2LSaACYSK6ZzTwUcl8jiwVCWSA_sleaEn0P6d97Nu0mBFbiz7ASS-ASGK1lrRzXU0jrNLtljJhKGlGU8gdTAv2OChS_rfF3e34e_Ed-qReqOeosbrBa92zGL3ukz4W5ISB5WeymtjO-WaVnfKWw","title":"os — Miscellaneous operating system interfaces — Python 3.15.2 documentation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html"}]}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 4 closes most of 74c. Two issues remain serious enough to block the build design. Publication or cleanup can remove another owner’s empty folder, and an ordinary database error can leave an empty output folder that blocks the next build.\n\n### 1. The 74c findings\n\n| Finding | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| One date rule | **Closed.** Both commands use `resolve_bound`. An explicit date on a legacy ledger can pass both commands, and a date after a recorded completed day is refused. For test 10, choose a legacy date later than its last judgement so the fixture distinguishes revision 4 from revision 3. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:107](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:107) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:306](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:306) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) |\n| `created_seq, rowid` order | **Closed.** Export and verification specify the same tie-breaker the existing library uses. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [bundle.py:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:232) |\n| Move preserves a folder the build did not create | **Open.** `mkdir` establishes who created the directory at that instant. The later `rename` replaces whichever empty directory occupies that name when it runs. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:133](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:133) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) |\n| Cleanup where the staging path is known | **Closed for the reported write failure.** `write_package` removes staging if either write fails before it returns the path. After it returns, the caller knows the path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:137](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:137) |\n| Outcome after publication | **Closed.** A report-write failure leaves the checked package in place, returns exit 2, and directs the user to `check`. The regenerated report marks the original export time as unmeasured. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:169](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:169) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) |\n| Test 12 through the real command | **Closed.** The unchanged command succeeds. The writer fault then gives the specific refusal and leaves no output or staging folder. Removing only the staged check lets the bad package reach the destination. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:309](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:309) |\n| Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 | **9, 13 and 15 closed.** Test 9 permits unrelated staging. Test 13 removes the matching source and refreshes the hash, so a checker that silently drops a missing item would accept the pair. Test 15 puts the genuine value last and refreshes the hash, isolating duplicate-name detection. **14 partly closed.** It overlaps two builds, but its empty-folder case occurs before the claim. Its later case uses a nonempty folder. Neither exercises a different *empty* folder at publication. Also, direct calls to module functions cannot establish the command’s claimed exit status. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:301](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:301) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:315](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:315) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:318](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:318) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:324](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:324) |\n\n### 2. What must change before building\n\n1. **Preserve the directory that actually occupies `--out`.** Suppose A is still checking its package. Someone mistakes its empty output folder for the crash debris described in the design and removes it. B then claims the same name. If A finishes first, its `rename` replaces B’s empty folder. If A encounters a refusal first, its `rmdir` deletes B’s empty folder. Errno 66 protects a folder containing a file. Both operations succeed in the empty-folder case. On this Mac, I recommend staging privately and using `renamex_np(..., RENAME_EXCL)` through Python’s standard-library `ctypes`, with refusal on filesystems that lack support. That removes the need to create or clean up a public claim. The decisive test puts a foreign empty directory at `--out` **after staging**, then verifies that publication refuses and that the same directory survives cleanup. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:134) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:209](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:209) · [macOS `rename(2)`:139](/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk/usr/share/man/man2/rename.2:139) · [Python `os.rename` and `os.rmdir`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.rename)\n\n2. **Clean up on a database failure before publication.** Revision 4 claims `--out` before reading the items database, but specifies cleanup only for `ReleaseRefused` and `OSError`. I verified in memory that querying a database without an `items` table raises `sqlite3.OperationalError`, outside both named cases. As written, that leaves an empty `--out` after an ordinary command failure, and a corrected retry refuses because the folder exists. Put cleanup of private staging in a `finally` covering its lifetime. The decisive command test uses a valid ledger and an items database missing that table, checks that the database error is reported, then retries successfully at the same output path with the correct database. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:93](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:93) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:159) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:167) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:204)"}}
